AnnIFs(Ideal,RingElement) -- the annihilating ideal of f^s for an arbitrary D-module
************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note AnnIFs: AnnIFs_lpIdeal_cmRingElement_rp,
  * Usage: 
        AnnIFs(I,f)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, that represents a holonomic
                                                                            
        D-module A /I (the ideal is expected to be f-saturated; one may use
                  n
        *note WeylClosure: WeylClosure, if it is not)
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a polynomial in a
                                                                              
        Weyl algebra A  (should contain no differential variables)
                      n
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the annihilating ideal of
        A_n[f^{-1},s] f^s tensored with A_n/I over the ring of polynomials

Description
===========

+-----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : W = QQ[x,dx, WeylAlgebra=>{x=>dx}]        |
|                                               |
|o1 = W                                         |
|                                               |
|o1 : PolynomialRing, 1 differential variable(s)|
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : AnnIFs (ideal dx, x^2)                    |
|                                               |
|o2 = ideal(x*dx - 2s)                          |
|                                               |
|o2 : Ideal of QQ[x, dx, s]                     |
+-----------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

Caveats and known problems: The ring of f should not have any parameters: it
should be a pure Weyl algebra. Similarly, this ring should not be a homogeneous
Weyl algebra.

See also
========

  * *note AnnFs: AnnFs, -- differential annihilator of a polynomial in a Weyl
    algebra
  * *note WeylAlgebra: (Macaulay2Doc)monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmWeylAlgebra=>_pd_pd_
    pd_rp, -- specify differential operators in the ring
  * *note WeylClosure: WeylClosure, -- Weyl closure of an ideal

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note AnnIFs(Ideal,RingElement): AnnIFs_lpIdeal_cmRingElement_rp, -- the
    annihilating ideal of f^s for an arbitrary D-module
