bFunction(...,Strategy=>...) -- specify strategy for computing b-function
*************************************************************************

Description
===========

  * IntRing -- the simplest algorithm available. The idea is to compute
                                                                       
    in      (I)  intersect it with k[t ,...,t ](t  = x D )Call the ideal
      (-w,w)                          1      n   i    i i               
    obtained J. Finally J + (t  + ... + t - s) \cap k[s] is generated by the
                              1          n
    b-function that we are looking for.
  * TryGeneric -- checks whether the ideal is generic and if that is the case
    uses Alg.5.1.5 in Saito-Sturmfels-Takayama (1999) otherwise is equivalent
    to NonGeneric
  * NonGeneric -- uses 5.1.6 in Saito-Sturmfels-Takayama (1999)
  * Default:IntRing

