bFunction(Ideal,List) -- b-function of an ideal
***********************************************

  * Function: *note bFunction: bFunction,
  * Usage: 
        b = bFunction(I,w)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, a holonomic ideal in the Weyl
                                                                              
        algebra A (K).
                 n
      * w, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of integer weights
        corresponding to the differential variables in the Weyl algebra.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Strategy: bFunction_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStrategy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value IntRing, specify strategy for computing b-function
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a polynomial b(s)
        which is the b-function of I with respect to w

Description
===========

Use *note setHomSwitch: (WeylAlgebras)setHomSwitch,(true) to force all the
subroutines to use homogenized *note WeylAlgebra:
(Macaulay2Doc)monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmWeylAlgebra=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,

Definition. The b-function b(s) is defined as the monic generator of the
                                                                        
intersection of in      (I) and K[s], where s = [w t  + ... + w t ] (here t  =
                  (-w,w)                          1 1          n n         i  
x D ).
 i i

+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x_1,x_2,D_1,D_2,WeylAlgebra=>{x_1=>D_1,x_2=>D_2}]|
|                                                             |
|o1 = R                                                       |
|                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing, 2 differential variable(s)              |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x_1, D_2-1)                                   |
|                                                             |
|o2 = ideal (x , D  - 1)                                      |
|             1   2                                           |
|                                                             |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                              |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : bFunction(I,{1, 0})                                     |
|                                                             |
|o3 = s + 1                                                   |
|                                                             |
|o3 : QQ[s]                                                   |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

The ring of I should not have any parameters: it should be a pure Weyl algebra.
Similarly, this ring should not be a homogeneous *note WeylAlgebra:
(Macaulay2Doc)monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmWeylAlgebra=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,

