bFunction(Module,List,List) -- b-function of a holonomic D-module
*****************************************************************

  * Function: *note bFunction: bFunction,
  * Usage: 
        b = bFunction(M,w,m)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, a holonomic module over a
                                                                           
        Weyl algebra A (K)
                      n
      * w, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of integer weights
        corresponding to the differential variables in the Weyl algebra
      * m, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of integers, each of which
        is the shift for the corresponding component
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Strategy: bFunction_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStrategy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value IntRing, specify strategy for computing b-function
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a polynomial b(s)
        which is the b-function of M with respect to w and m

Description
===========

The algorithm represents M as F/N where F is free and N is a submodule of F.
                                                                            
Then it computes b-functions b (s) for N \cap F  (i-th component of F) and
                              i                i                          
outputs lcm{ b (s-m ) }
              i    i
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x, dx, WeylAlgebra => {x=>dx}]                       |
|                                                                 |
|o1 = R                                                           |
|                                                                 |
|o1 : PolynomialRing, 1 differential variable(s)                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : M = cokernel matrix {{x^2, 0, 0}, {0, dx^3, 0}, {0, 0, x^3}}|
|                                                                 |
|o2 = cokernel | x2 0    0  |                                     |
|              | 0  dx^3 0  |                                     |
|              | 0  0    x3 |                                     |
|                                                                 |
|                            3                                    |
|o2 : R-module, quotient of R                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : factorBFunction bFunction(M, {1}, {0,0,0})                  |
|                                                                 |
|o3 = (s)(s - 2)(s - 1)(s + 1)(s + 2)(s + 3)                      |
|                                                                 |
|o3 : Expression of class Product                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : factorBFunction bFunction(M, {1}, {1,2,3})                  |
|                                                                 |
|o4 = (s)(s - 4)(s - 3)(s - 2)(s - 1)(s + 1)                      |
|                                                                 |
|o4 : Expression of class Product                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

The Weyl algebra should not have any parameters. Similarly, it should not be a
homogeneous Weyl algebra

See also
========

  * *note globalBFunction: globalBFunction_lpRingElement_rp, -- global
    b-function (else known as the Bernstein-Sato polynomial)
  * *note factorBFunction: factorBFunction_lpRingElement_rp, -- factorization
    of a b-function

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note bFunction(Module,List,List): bFunction_lpModule_cmList_cmList_rp, --
    b-function of a holonomic D-module
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

