Ddual -- holonomic dual of a D-module
*************************************

  * Usage: 
        Ddual M, Ddual I
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, over the Weyl algebra D
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, which represents the module M
        = D/I
  * Outputs:
      * a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, the holonomic dual of M

Description
===========

                                           n                           
If M is a holonomic left D-module, then Ext  (M,D) is a holonomic right
                                            D                          
                                                                            
D-module.  The holonomic dual is defined to be the left module associated to
                                                                            
   n
Ext  (M,D).  The dual is obtained by computing a free resolution of M,
    D
dualizing, and applying the standard transposition to the n-th homology.
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : I = AppellF1({1,0,-3,2})                                                |
|                                                                             |
|               3  2    2           2  2                 2                    |
|o1 = ideal (- x Dx  - x y*Dx*Dy + x Dx  + x*y*Dx*Dy - 2x Dx + 2x*Dx, -       |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|        2         3  2                2  2              2                    |
|     x*y Dx*Dy - y Dy  + x*y*Dx*Dy + y Dy  + 3x*y*Dx + y Dy + 2y*Dy + 3y,    |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     x*Dx*Dy - y*Dx*Dy + 3Dx)                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : Ideal of QQ[x, y, Dx, Dy]                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : Ddual I                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = cokernel | 0  xDy-yDy-4 x2Dx+y2Dy-xDx-yDy+x+4y                          |
|              | Dx -yDy-1    0                                               |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : QQ[x, y, Dx, Dy]-module, quotient of (QQ[x, y,                          |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|y2DxDy+y2Dy^2-yDxDy-yDy^2+4xDx+4yDx+5yDy-4Dx+4 0                           | |
|0                                              y3Dy^2-y2Dy^2+7y2Dy-2yDy+5y | |
|                                                                             |
|        2                                                                    |
|Dx, Dy])                                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

The input module M should be holonomic.  The user should check this manually
with the script Ddim.

See also
========

  * *note Ddim: (WeylAlgebras)Ddim, -- dimension of a D-module
  * *note Dtransposition: (WeylAlgebras)Dtransposition, -- standard
    transposition for Weyl algebra

