deRhamAll(RingElement) -- deRham complex for the complement of a hypersurface
*****************************************************************************

  * Function: *note deRhamAll: deRhamAll_lpRingElement_rp,
  * Usage: 
        deRhamAll f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Strategy: deRhamAll_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStrategy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value Schreyer,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, containing explicit
        cohomology classes in the deRham complex for the complement of the
        hypersurface {f = 0} and supplementary information

Description
===========

The routine deRhamAll can be used to compute cup product structures as in the
paper 'The cup product structure for complements of affine varieties' by
Walther(2000).


For a more basic functionality see *note deRham: deRham,.
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y]                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : f = x^2-y^3                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|        3    2                                                               |
|o2 = - y  + x                                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : R                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : deRhamAll f                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                        2      1                             |
|o3 = HashTable{BFunction => (s - 1)(s - -)(s - -)                            |
|                                        3      3                             |
|                                                    1                        |
|               CohomologyGroups => HashTable{0 => QQ }                       |
|                                                    1                        |
|                                             1 => QQ                         |
|                                             2 => 0                          |
|               LocalizeMap => | -x_2^3+x_1^2 |                               |
|                                               1                         2   |
|               OmegaRes => (QQ[x ..x , D ..D ])  <-- (QQ[x ..x , D ..D ])    |
|                                1   2   1   2             1   2   1   2      |
|                                                                             |
|                           0                         1                       |
|               PreCycles => HashTable{0 => | 0 |}                            |
|                                           | 1 |                             |
|                                      1 => | 0 |                             |
|                                           | 1 |                             |
|                                           | 0 |                             |
|                                      2 => 0                                 |
|               TransferCycles => HashTable{0 => | 3x_2^3-3x_1^2 |}           |
|                                           1 => | 2x_1   |                   |
|                                                | 3x_2^2 |                   |
|                                           2 => 0                            |
|                                                  1                          |
|               VResolution => (QQ[x ..x , D ..D ])  <-- (QQ[x ..x , D ..D    |
|                                   1   2   1   2             1   2   1   2   |
|                                                                             |
|                              0                         1                    |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : HashTable                                                               |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                                   }                                         |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                         1                                                   |
| <-- (QQ[x ..x , D ..D ])  <-- 0                                             |
|          1   2   1   2                                                      |
|                               3                                             |
|     2                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|  3                         2                                                |
|])  <-- (QQ[x ..x , D ..D ])  <-- 0                                          |
|             1   2   1   2                                                   |
|                                  3                                          |
|        2                                                                    |
