DExt -- Ext groups between holonomic modules
********************************************

  * Usage: 
        DExt(M,N), DExt(M,N,w)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, over the Weyl algebra D
      * N, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, over the Weyl algebra D
      * w, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a positive weight vector
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Info: DExt_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmInfo=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ..., default
        value 1,
      * *note Output: DExt_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmOutput=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ..., default
        value HomologyModules,
      * *note Special: DExt_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmSpecial=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value None,
      * *note Strategy: DExt_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStrategy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value Schreyer,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,,  the Ext groups between
        holonomic D-modulesM and N

Description
===========

The Ext groups between D-modules M and N are the derived functors of Hom, and
are finite-dimensional vector spaces over the ground field when M and N are
holonomic.

The procedure calls *note Drestriction: Drestriction,, which uses w if
specified.

The algorithm used appears in the paper 'Polynomial and rational solutions of
holonomic systems' by Oaku-Takayama-Tsai (2000). The method is to combine
isomorphisms of Bjork and Kashiwara with the restriction algorithm.

+-----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : W = QQ[x, D, WeylAlgebra=>{x=>D}]         |
|                                               |
|o1 = W                                         |
|                                               |
|o1 : PolynomialRing, 1 differential variable(s)|
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : M = W^1/ideal(x*(D-1))                    |
|                                               |
|o2 = cokernel | xD-x |                         |
|                                               |
|                            1                  |
|o2 : W-module, quotient of W                   |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : N = W^1/ideal((D-1)^2)                    |
|                                               |
|o3 = cokernel | D2-2D+1 |                      |
|                                               |
|                            1                  |
|o3 : W-module, quotient of W                   |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i4 : DExt(M,N)                                 |
|                                               |
|                      2                        |
|o4 = HashTable{0 => QQ }                       |
|                      2                        |
|               1 => QQ                         |
|                                               |
|o4 : HashTable                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

Input modules M, N should be holonomic.Does not yet compute explicit
representations of Ext groups such as Yoneda representation.

See also
========

  * *note DHom: DHom, -- D-homomorphisms between holonomic D-modules
  * *note Drestriction: Drestriction, -- restriction modules of a D-module

Ways to use DExt:
=================

  * "DExt(Module,Module)"
  * "DExt(Module,Module,List)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note DExt: DExt, is a *note method function with options:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

