DintegrationIdeal -- integration ideal of a D-module
****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        DintegrationIdeal(I,w)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, which represents the module M
        = D/I
      * w, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a weight vector
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Strategy: DintegrationIdeal_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStrategy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,
        => ..., default value Schreyer,
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the integration ideal of M w.r.t.
        the weight vector w

Description
===========

A supplementary function for *note Dintegration: Dintegration, that computes
the integration ideal.
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : W = QQ[y,t,Dy,Dt, WeylAlgebra => {y=>Dy, t=>Dt}];               |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(2*t*Dy+Dt, t*Dt+2*y*Dy+2); -- annihilator of 1/(t^2-y)|
|                                                                     |
|o2 : Ideal of W                                                      |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : DintegrationIdeal(I, {1,4})                                     |
|                                                                     |
|o3 = ideal 1                                                         |
|                                                                     |
|o3 : Ideal of QQ                                                     |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

The module M should be specializable to the subspace. This is true for
holonomic modules.The weight vector w should be a list of n numbers if M is a
module over the nth Weyl algebra.

See also
========

  * *note Dintegration: Dintegration, -- integration modules of a D-module
  * *note DintegrationAll: DintegrationAll, -- integration modules of a
    D-module (extended version)
  * *note Drestriction: Drestriction, -- restriction modules of a D-module

Ways to use DintegrationIdeal:
==============================

  * "DintegrationIdeal(Ideal,List)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note DintegrationIdeal: DintegrationIdeal, is a *note method
function with options: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

