factorBFunction(RingElement) -- factorization of a b-function
*************************************************************

  * Function: *note factorBFunction: factorBFunction_lpRingElement_rp,
  * Usage: 
        bFunction b
  * Inputs:
      * b, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a polynomial
        obtained via one of the b-function routines
  * Outputs:
      * a *note product expression: (Macaulay2Doc)Product,, the factorization
        of b

Description
===========

Fact. The roots of any b-function are rational.
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x, dx, WeylAlgebra => {x=>dx}]                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing, 1 differential variable(s)                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : f = x^10                                                                |
|                                                                             |
|      10                                                                     |
|o2 = x                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : R                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : b = globalBFunction f                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|      10   11 9   66 8   363 7   157773 6   180411 5   341693 4   16819 3    |
|o3 = s   + --s  + --s  + ---s  + ------s  + ------s  + ------s  + -----s  +  |
|            2      5      20      10000      20000     100000     20000      |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|      1594197 2    66429       567                                           |
|     --------s  + -------s + -------                                         |
|     12500000     6250000    1562500                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : QQ[s]                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : factorBFunction b                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|                 1      1      2      3      4       1       3       7       |
|o4 = (s + 1)(s + -)(s + -)(s + -)(s + -)(s + -)(s + --)(s + --)(s + --)(s +  |
|                 2      5      5      5      5      10      10      10       |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : Expression of class Product                                             |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| 9                                                                           |
|--)                                                                          |
|10                                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

f should be an output of one of the b-function routines

See also
========

  * *note bFunction: bFunction, -- b-function
