generalB(List,RingElement) -- global generalized Bernstein-Sato polynomial
**************************************************************************

  * Function: *note generalB: generalB_lpList_cmRingElement_rp,
  * Usage: 
        b = generalB(F,g), b = generalB F
  * Inputs:
      * F, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of polynomials
      * g, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a polynomial
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Exponent: generalB_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmExponent=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value null, specify exponent m for m-generalized Bernstein-Sato
        polynomial
      * *note Strategy: generalB_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStrategy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value InitialIdeal, specify strategy for computing generalized
        Bernstein-Sato polynomial
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the general
        Bernstein-Sato polynomial b(s) in Q[s]

Description
===========

Bernstein-Sato polynomial for an arbitrary affine variety was introduced in
Budur, Mustata, and Saito ``Bernstein--Sato polynomials of arbitrary
varieties''. If the option *note Exponent:
generalB_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmExponent=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, is specified, then the
m-generalized Bernstein-Sato polynomial is computed. See Berkesch and Leykin
``Algorithms for Bernstein-Sato polynomials and multiplier ideals'' for
definitions.
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : W = makeWA(QQ[x_1..x_3]);                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : factorBFunction generalB ({x_2^2-x_1*x_3, x_1^3-x_3^2}, x_2)            |
|                                                                             |
|                 5      9      11      11      13      29      31      35    |
|o2 = (s + 2)(s + -)(s + -)(s + --)(s + --)(s + --)(s + --)(s + --)(s + --)(s |
|                 2      4       4       6       6      12      12      12    |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Expression of class Product                                             |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|  37                                                                         |
|+ --)                                                                        |
|  12                                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

The input could be either in a polynomial ring or the Weyl algebra. In the
latter case the algebra should not have any central variables and should not be
a homogeneous Weyl algebra.

See also
========

  * *note bFunction: bFunction, -- b-function
  * *note globalBFunction: globalBFunction_lpRingElement_rp, -- global
    b-function (else known as the Bernstein-Sato polynomial)
  * *note lct: lct_lpIdeal_rp, -- compute the log canonical threshold for an
    ideal
  * *note multiplierIdeal: multiplierIdeal_lpIdeal_cmQQ_rp, -- multiplier ideal

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * "generalB(List)"
  * *note generalB(List,RingElement): generalB_lpList_cmRingElement_rp, --
    global generalized Bernstein-Sato polynomial
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

