globalB(Ideal,RingElement) -- compute global b-function and b-operator for a D-module and a polynomial
******************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note globalB: globalB_lpIdeal_cmRingElement_rp,
  * Usage: 
        H = globalB(I,f)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, a holonomic ideal
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a polynomial in a
        Weyl algebra (should not contain differential variables)
  * Outputs:
      * H, a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, containing the keys
        Bpolynomial and Boperator

Description
===========

The algorithm used here is a modification of the original algorithm of Oaku for
computing Bernstein-Sato polynomials
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x, dx, WeylAlgebra => {x=>dx}]                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing, 1 differential variable(s)                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : f = x^7                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|      7                                                                      |
|o2 = x                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : R                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : b = globalB(ideal dx, f)                                                |
|                                                                             |
|                              7                                              |
|o3 = HashTable{Boperator => dx                                               |
|                                     7           6           5           4   |
|               Bpolynomial => 823543s  + 3294172s  + 5411854s  + 4705960s  + |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : HashTable                                                               |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                                    }                                        |
|        3          2                                                         |
|2321767s  + 643468s  + 91476s + 5040                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : factorBFunction b.Bpolynomial                                           |
|                                                                             |
|                 1      2      3      4      5      6                        |
|o4 = (s + 1)(s + -)(s + -)(s + -)(s + -)(s + -)(s + -)                       |
|                 7      7      7      7      7      7                        |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : Expression of class Product                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note bFunction: bFunction, -- b-function
  * *note globalBFunction: globalBFunction_lpRingElement_rp, -- global
    b-function (else known as the Bernstein-Sato polynomial)
  * *note factorBFunction: factorBFunction_lpRingElement_rp, -- factorization
    of a b-function

Ways to use this method:
========================

