globalBFunction(RingElement) -- global b-function (else known as the Bernstein-Sato polynomial)
***********************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note globalBFunction: globalBFunction_lpRingElement_rp,
  * Usage: 
        b = globalBFunction f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a polynomial
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Strategy: globalBFunction_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStrategy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,
        => ..., default value GeneralBernsteinSato, specify strategy for
        computing global b-function
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the b-function
        b(s) in Q[s]

Description
===========

Definition. Let D = A_{2n}(K) = K<x_1,...,x_n,d_1,...,d_n> be a Weyl algebra.
The Bernstein-Sato polynomial of a polynomial f is defined to be the monic
generator of the ideal of all polynomials b(s) in K[s] such that  b(s) f^s =
Q(s,x,d) f^{s+1} where Q lives in D[s].

Algorithm. Let I_f = D<t,dt>*<t-f, d_1+df/dx_1*dt, ..., d_n+df/dx_n*dt> Let
B(s) = bFunction(I, {1, 0, ..., 0}) where 1 in the weight that corresponds to
dt. Then the global b-function is b_f = B(-s-1)

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x]                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : f = x^10                                                                |
|                                                                             |
|      10                                                                     |
|o2 = x                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : R                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : b = globalBFunction f                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|      10   11 9   66 8   363 7   157773 6   180411 5   341693 4   16819 3    |
|o3 = s   + --s  + --s  + ---s  + ------s  + ------s  + ------s  + -----s  +  |
|            2      5      20      10000      20000     100000     20000      |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|      1594197 2    66429       567                                           |
|     --------s  + -------s + -------                                         |
|     12500000     6250000    1562500                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : QQ[s]                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : factorBFunction b                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|                 1      1      2      3      4       1       3       7       |
|o4 = (s + 1)(s + -)(s + -)(s + -)(s + -)(s + -)(s + --)(s + --)(s + --)(s +  |
|                 2      5      5      5      5      10      10      10       |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : Expression of class Product                                             |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| 9                                                                           |
|--)                                                                          |
|10                                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

