IHmodule -- intersection (co)homology module of an irreducible closed subvariety
********************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        IHmodule(I)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, ideal in the polynomial ring
        $R$
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * LocCohomStrategy => a *note sequence: (Macaulay2Doc)Sequence,, default
        value (Walther,), (String, String); see *note
        localCohom(...,Strategy=>...):
        localCohom_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStrategy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, and *note
        localCohom(...,LocStrategy=>...):
        localCohom_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmLocStrategy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,
      * LocStrategy => a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, default value
        OTW, see *note Dlocalize(...,Strategy=>...):
        Dlocalize_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStrategy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,, or for regular
        sequence use CompleteIntersection
  * Outputs:
      * a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, the intersection cohomology
        $D$-module

Description
===========

This routine gives a presentation of the Brylinski-Kashiwara intersection
cohomology $D$-module of the closed subvariety defined by $I$. Via the
Riemann-Hilbert correspondence, this corresponds to the trivial local system on
the smooth locus of the variety.

+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R=QQ[x,y,z]                                                        |
|                                                                        |
|o1 = R                                                                  |
|                                                                        |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                                     |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I=ideal(x^2+y^3)                                                   |
|                                                                        |
|            3    2                                                      |
|o2 = ideal(y  + x )                                                     |
|                                                                        |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                                         |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : IHmodule(I)                                                        |
|                                                                        |
|o3 = subquotient (| 0  0  |, | dz -x 0  y2 -2ydy-6 0            |)      |
|                  | xy x2 |  | 0  y  dz x  -3ydx   -3xdx-2ydy-8 |       |
|                                                                        |
|                                                                       2|
|o3 : QQ[x..z, dx, dy, dz]-module, subquotient of (QQ[x..z, dx, dy, dz]) |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+

When the given generators of $I$ form a regular sequence, use
LocStrategy=>CompleteIntersection for a generally faster algorithm, which
implements the determination of the IC module in terms of the fundamental class
as described in: D. Barlet and M. Kashiwara, Le réseau $L^2$ d’un système
holonome régulier, Invent. Math. 86 (1986), no. 1, 35–62.

+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : R=QQ[x,y]                                                  |
|                                                                |
|o4 = R                                                          |
|                                                                |
|o4 : PolynomialRing                                             |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : I=ideal(x^2+y^3)                                           |
|                                                                |
|            3    2                                              |
|o5 = ideal(y  + x )                                             |
|                                                                |
|o5 : Ideal of R                                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : IHmodule(I, LocStrategy=>CompleteIntersection)             |
|                                                                |
|o6 = subquotient (| x |, | 3xdx+2ydy+6 3y2dx-2xdy y3+x2 |)      |
|                                                                |
|                                                               1|
|o6 : QQ[x..y, dx, dy]-module, subquotient of (QQ[x..y, dx, dy]) |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

Must be a ring of characteristic 0. The ideal $I$ should have only 1 minimal
prime.



Ways to use IHmodule:
=====================

  * "IHmodule(Ideal)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note IHmodule: IHmodule, is a *note method function with options:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

