isInMultiplierIdeal(RingElement,Ideal,QQ) -- multiplier ideal membership test
*****************************************************************************

  * Function: *note isInMultiplierIdeal:
    isInMultiplierIdeal_lpRingElement_cmIdeal_cmQQ_rp,
  * Usage: 
        b = isInMultiplierIdeal(g,I,c)
  * Inputs:
      * g, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a polynomial
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, an ideal in a polynomial ring
      * c, a *note rational number: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,, coefficient (or a list
        of coefficients)
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Strategy => ..., default value generalizedBFunction
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, answers: is in the
        multiplier ideal J_I(c)?

Description
===========

Test if the given polynomial is in the multiplier ideal for given ideal and
coefficient. In general, the test is cheaper than computing the whole
multiplier ideal.

There are two options for strategy:
  * generalizedBFunction -- via computation of the generalized Bernstein-Sato
    polynomial
  * mGeneralizedBFunction -- via computation of the m-generalized
    Bernstein-Sato polynomial
See Berkesch and Leykin ``Algorithms for Bernstein-Sato polynomials and
multiplier ideals'' for details.
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x_1..x_4];                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : isInMultiplierIdeal(x_1, ideal {x_1^3 - x_2^2, x_2^3 - x_3^2}, 31/18)   |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = false                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : isInMultiplierIdeal(x_1*x_2, ideal {x_1^3 - x_2^2, x_2^3 - x_3^2},      |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = true                                                                    |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|31/18)                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

