kOrderAnnFa -- k-th order D-annihilator of a power of a polynomial
******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        kOrderAnnFa(k,f,a)
        kOrderAnnFs(k,f)
  * Inputs:
      * k, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, positive
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a polynomial in
        $K[x_1,...,x_n]$
      * a, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, (usually negative) exponent
  * Outputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, an ideal in the Weyl algebra
        $K<x_1,...,x_n,\partial_1,...,\partial_n>$ (or
        $K[s]<x_1,...,x_n,\partial_1,...,\partial_n>$)

Description
===========

*note kOrderAnnFa: kOrderAnnFa, (*note kOrderAnnFs: kOrderAnnFa,) return an
ideal generated by elements of order at most $k$ of the annihilator of $f^a$
($f^s$). See [Castro-Jimenez, Leykin "Computing localizations iteratively"
(2012) (see https://arxiv.org/abs/1110.0182 )] for details.

+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x_1,x_2]; f = x_1^2-x_2^3;                                |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : A1 = kOrderAnnFa(1,f,-1)                                         |
|                                                                      |
|                                   2               3       2        2 |
|o3 = ideal (3x dx  + 2x dx  + 6, 3x dx  + 2x dx , x dx  - x dx  + 3x )|
|              1  1     2  2        2  1     1  2   2  2    1  2     2 |
|                                                                      |
|o3 : Ideal of QQ[x ..x , dx ..dx ]                                    |
|                  1   2    1    2                                     |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : As = kOrderAnnFs(1,f)                                            |
|                                                                      |
|              2                                                       |
|o4 = ideal (3x dx  + 2x dx , 6s - 3x dx  - 2x dx )                    |
|              2  1     1  2         1  1     2  2                     |
|                                                                      |
|o4 : Ideal of QQ[x ..x , dx ..dx , s]                                 |
|                  1   2    1    2                                     |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
