lct(Ideal) -- compute the log canonical threshold for an ideal
**************************************************************

  * Function: *note lct: lct_lpIdeal_rp,
  * Usage: 
        l = lct I
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, an ideal in a polynomial ring
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Strategy: lct_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStrategy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value GeneralBernsteinSato, specify strategy for computing lct
  * Outputs:
      * l, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a rational number,
        the log canonical threshold of I

Description
===========

+--------------------------------------------+
|i1 : QQ[x_1..x_3];                          |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal (x_2^2-x_1*x_3, x_1^3-x_3^2);|
|                                            |
|o2 : Ideal of QQ[x ..x ]                    |
|                  1   3                     |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i3 : lct I                                  |
|                                            |
|     17                                     |
|o3 = --                                     |
|     12                                     |
|                                            |
|o3 : QQ                                     |
+--------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note bFunction: bFunction, -- b-function
  * *note generalB: generalB_lpList_cmRingElement_rp, -- global generalized
    Bernstein-Sato polynomial

Ways to use this method:
========================

