localBFunction(RingElement,Ideal) -- local b-function (a.k.a. the local Bernstein-Sato polynomial)
**************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note localBFunction: localBFunction_lpRingElement_cmIdeal_rp,
  * Usage: 
        b = localBFunction(f,P)
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a polynomial
      * P, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, a (prime) ideal
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the local
        b-function b_P(s) in Q[s]

Description
===========

Computes the local b-function of f at P, if P is a prime ideal.

+--------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y]; f = x^2*(x+y+1); P = ideal(x,y);|
|                                                  |
|o3 : Ideal of R                                   |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : b = localBFunction(f,P)                      |
|                                                  |
|      2   3    1                                  |
|o4 = s  + -s + -                                  |
|          2    2                                  |
|                                                  |
|o4 : QQ[s]                                        |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : factorBFunction b                            |
|                                                  |
|                 1                                |
|o5 = (s + 1)(s + -)                               |
|                 2                                |
|                                                  |
|o5 : Expression of class Product                  |
+--------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

(feature) If P is not prime, computes the lcm of local b-functions over all
primes containing P

