File: BernsteinSato.info, Node: localCohom_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStrategy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, Next: localCohom_lpIdeal_rp, Prev: localCohom_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmLocStrategy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, Up: Top

localCohom(...,Strategy=>...) -- specify strategy for local cohomology
**********************************************************************

Description
===========

There are two main strategies, Walther and OaTa. If the user selects Walther,
which is the default, then *note LocStrategy: LocStrategy, determines the
localization strategy for localCohom(...Ideal...) and localCohom(...Ideal,
Module...).
  * Walther -- the algorithm of U. Walther that uses Cech complex.
  *   * LocStrategy => null -- used only for localCohom(...Ideal...),
        localizations are done by straightforward computation of annihilators
        and b-polynomials as described in [1].
      * LocStrategy => OaTaWa -- localizations are done following
        Oaku-Takayama-Walther method [2].
      * LocStrategy => Oaku -- localizations are done following Oaku's
        algorithm.
  * OaTa -- restriction from the graph embedding is used, which is due to T.
    Oaku and N. Takayama [3]. See *note Drestriction: Drestriction,.
For detailed description of the algorithms see
  * [1] Walther, Algorithmic computation of local cohomology modules and the
    local cohomological dimension of algebraic varieties (JPAA (139), 1999.)
  * [2] Oaku, Takayama, Walther, A Localization Algorithm for D-modules (J.
    Symbolic Computation (29), 2000.)
  * [3] Oaku, Takayama, Algorithms for D-modules -- restriction, tensor
    product, localization, and local cohomology groups (JPAA (156), 2001.)

Caveat
======

localCohom(...Ideal, Module...) with the default strategy computes
presentations for all the terms in the Cech complex regardless of the requested
homological degrees. All strategies use the given generators of the ideal; the
user is advised to call *note mingens: (Macaulay2Doc)mingens, before calling
localCohom.

Functions with optional argument named Strategy:
================================================

  * "addHook(...,Strategy=>...)" -- see *note addHook: (Macaulay2Doc)addHook,
    -- add a hook function to an object for later processing
  * "annihilator(...,Strategy=>...)" -- see *note annihilator:
    (Saturation)annihilator, -- the annihilator ideal
  * "basis(...,Strategy=>...)" -- see *note basis: (Macaulay2Doc)basis, --
