paramBpoly(RingElement,File) -- compute the list of all possible Bernstein-Sato polynomials for a parametric polynomial
***********************************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note paramBpoly: paramBpoly_lpRingElement_cmFile_rp,
  * Usage: 
        paramBpoly(f,file)
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a polynomial in
        Weyl algebra A_n(Q)
      * file, a *note file: (Macaulay2Doc)File,, a file for TeX output (or
        stdio)
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * ground field
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, all possible Bernstein-Sato
        polynomials

Description
===========

This function computes the finite list of all possible Bernstein-Sato
polynomials for a polynomial with parametric coefficients and creates latex
code describing strata in the parameter space corresponding to the B.-S.
polynomials --- each stratum is a constructible set. This is an implementation
of the algorithmic approach in Anton Leykin. Constructibility of the Set of
Polynomials with a Fixed Bernstein-Sato Polynomial: an Algorithmic Approach.
Journal of Symbolic Computation, 32(6):663–675, 2001.
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : A =  (QQ [a,b,c]) [x, y, Dx, Dy, WeylAlgebra => {x=>Dx, y=>Dy}]|
|                                                                    |
|o1 = A                                                              |
|                                                                    |
|o1 : PolynomialRing, 2 differential variable(s)                     |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : paramBpoly(a*x^2 + b*x*y + c*y^2, stdio)                       |
|\begin{itemize}                                                     |
|\item $b(s)=(S+1)^2$ corresponds to                                 |
|$V(0)$$\setminus$$V(b^2-4*a*c)$                                     |
|\item $b(s)=(S+1/2)*(S+1)$ corresponds to                           |
|$V(b^2-4*a*c)$                                                      |
|\end{itemize}                                                       |
|                                                                    |
|             2       1                                              |
|o2 = {(S + 1) , (S + -)(S + 1)}                                     |
|                     2                                              |
|                                                                    |
|o2 : List                                                           |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

A finite field ZZ/p is used to speed up computations. Option "ground field" may
be used to change the characteristic p. If p=0 the computation will be
attempted over QQ.

See also
========

  * *note globalBFunction: globalBFunction_lpRingElement_rp, -- global
    b-function (else known as the Bernstein-Sato polynomial)

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note paramBpoly(RingElement,File): paramBpoly_lpRingElement_cmFile_rp, --
    compute the list of all possible Bernstein-Sato polynomials for a
    parametric polynomial
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

