polynomialAnnihilator -- annihilator of a polynomial in the Weyl algebra
************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        polynomialAnnihilator f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, polynomial
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the annihilating (left) ideal of
        f in the Weyl algebra

Description
===========

+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : makeWA(QQ[x,y])                                          |
|                                                              |
|o1 = QQ[x..y, dx, dy]                                         |
|                                                              |
|o1 : PolynomialRing, 2 differential variable(s)               |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : f = x^2-y^3                                              |
|                                                              |
|        3    2                                                |
|o2 = - y  + x                                                 |
|                                                              |
|o2 : QQ[x..y, dx, dy]                                         |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : I = polynomialAnnihilator f                              |
|                                                              |
|               3      2            3      2       2    4    4 |
|o3 = ideal (- y dx + x dx - 2x, - y dy + x dy + 3y , dx , dy )|
|                                                              |
|o3 : Ideal of QQ[x..y, dx, dy]                                |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

The input f should be an element of a Weyl algebra, and not an element of a
commutative polynomial ring. However, f should only involve commutative
variables.

