polynomialExt -- Ext groups between a holonomic module and a polynomial ring
****************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        polynomialExt M, polynomialExt I; rationalFunctionExt(i,M), rationalFunctionExt(i,I)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, over the Weyl algebra D
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, which represents the module M
        = D/I
      * i, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, nonnegative
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Strategy: polynomialExt_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStrategy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value Schreyer,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable, or a *note module:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, the Ext^i group(s) between holonomic M and the
        polynomial ring

Description
===========

The Ext groups between a D-module M and the polynomial ring are the derived
functors of Hom, and are finite-dimensional vector spaces over the ground field
when M is holonomic.

The algorithm used appears in the paper 'Polynomial and rational solutions of
holonomic systems' by Oaku-Takayama-Tsai (2000). The method is to combine
isomorphisms of Bjork and Kashiwara with the restriction algorithm.

+-----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : W = QQ[x, D, WeylAlgebra=>{x=>D}]         |
|                                               |
|o1 = W                                         |
|                                               |
|o1 : PolynomialRing, 1 differential variable(s)|
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : M = W^1/ideal(x^2*D^2)                    |
|                                               |
|o2 = cokernel | x2D2 |                         |
|                                               |
|                            1                  |
|o2 : W-module, quotient of W                   |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : polynomialExt(M)                          |
|                                               |
|                      2                        |
|o3 = HashTable{0 => QQ }                       |
|                      2                        |
|               1 => QQ                         |
|                                               |
|o3 : HashTable                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

Does not yet compute explicit representations of Ext groups such as Yoneda
representation.

See also
========

  * *note polynomialSolutions: polynomialSolutions, -- polynomial solutions of
    a holonomic system
  * *note rationalFunctionExt: rationalFunctionExt, -- Ext(holonomic D-module,
    polynomial ring localized at the singular locus)
  * *note DExt: DExt, -- Ext groups between holonomic modules
  * *note Dintegration: Dintegration, -- integration modules of a D-module

Ways to use polynomialExt:
==========================

  * "polynomialExt(Ideal)"
  * "polynomialExt(Module)"
  * "polynomialExt(ZZ,Ideal)"
  * "polynomialExt(ZZ,Module)"

