reiffen -- Reiffen's curve
**************************

  * Usage: 
        reiffen(p,q)
  * Inputs:
      * p, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * q, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the defining
        polynomial of Reiffen's (p,q)-curve

Description
===========

Reiffen's (p,q)-curve is a singular curve defined by $f_{p,q} =
x_1^p+x_2^q+x_1x_2^{q-1} = 0$ for $p>=4$ and $q>=p+1$.

+-------------------+
|i1 : reiffen(4,5)  |
|                   |
|        4    5    4|
|o1 = x x  + x  + x |
|      1 2    2    1|
|                   |
|o1 : QQ[x ..x ]    |
|         1   2     |
+-------------------+

Ways to use reiffen:
====================

  * "reiffen(ZZ,ZZ)"

For the programmer
==================

